content.text:
Now CSS for cmd-footer/confirm/back and target wrapper. Also mobile adjustments.

Add after `.cmd-desc b` maybe:

```
.cmd-footer{display:flex;gap:6px;margin-top:8px;}
.cmd-confirm,.cmd-back{
 display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;flex:1;
 padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid rgba(160,180,210,.2);background:rgba(255,255,255,.03);
 color:#ded9ca;font-size:16px;cursor:pointer;transition:all .1s;
}
.cmd-confirm{border-color:var(--gold-dim);color:#fff3d3;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(231,199,123,.16),rgba(231,199,123,.04));}
.cmd-confirm:hover{...}
.cmd-confirm .key{font-family:var(--pixel);font-size:7px;color:var(--gold);opacity:.8;}
.cmd-back{flex:0 0 auto;color:var(--muted);}
```

Target:
```
.target-cards{display:flex;gap:8px;}
.target-actions{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;justify-content:stretch;}
.target-actions .cmd-confirm,.target-actions .cmd-back{flex:1;min-width:104px;padding:6px 10px;}
```
`.target-layer` currently flex; fine. Mobile smaller.

Also `.battle-command.with-party` on desktop? It only applies mobile. With footer, panel height increases by ~40px; may overlap party HUD? Panel bottom left width 500, party right 252; okay at 1280. On mobile, `.battle-command.with-party{width:62vw}` and max-height 44vh with overflow auto; footer may need scroll. Since panel is bottom 10 with max-height 44vh (portrait 371px), content ~ head 20 + grid 3*? 2 cols → 3 rows*34=102 + desc 28 + footer 36 = ~200, fits. Landscape 360h → 158 max-height; content 200 → scroll; confirm button at bottom of scroll could be off-screen requiring scroll. Better on mobile make max-height 52vh and compact; or make footer sticky. Add `.cmd-footer{position:sticky;bottom:0;background:...}`? Since `.battle-command` is the scroll container, sticky bottom works if padding. Simpler: `.battle-command{max-height:52vh}` and footer compact; landscape 360*0.52=187, still scroll. Sticky footer ensures confirm always visible. Add `.cmd-footer{position:sticky;bottom:-8px;padding-top:6px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,transparent,rgba(6,11,22,.96) 30%);}` Hmm sticky within overflow auto. Good.

But `with-party` 62vw on mobile means width ~242px; two buttons side by side each ~110px; fine. Let's make back button only in skill/item (not root) to save space; root only confirm.

Also add touch confirm visible anyway.

Add CSS.

