Implement media max-width 520 (portrait-ish):
```
@media (max-width:520px){
  .battle-party{left:10px;right:10px;bottom:max(10px,env(safe-area-inset-bottom));width:auto;flex-direction:row;gap:5px;}
  .battle-unit{flex:1 1 0;min-width:0;grid-template-columns:22px 1fr;gap:5px;padding:4px 5px;}
  .battle-unit .bu-face{width:22px;height:22px;}
  .bu-name{font-size:5px;}
  .bu-name span{font-size:11px;}
  .bu-status{display:none;}
  .battle-command{left:10px;right:10px;bottom:calc(max(10px,env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) + 54px);width:auto;max-height:52vh;}
  .battle-command.with-party{width:auto;}
  .turn-order{top:86px;right:10px;bottom:auto;}
}
```
But turn order 6 chips width 94? 6 chips * 34 + gaps = 250 wide, at top right would extend left across screen (fine) but may overlap battle log (top 14..80). Top 86 is below log. Could stay at bottom? Command now occupies bottom 64..~500; turn order at bottom 210 overlaps command. Move to top 86 right 10. On 390, turn order width 94? In screenshot turn-order width 94 because it had 3 chips (Guarda x2 + Kael). 6 would be ~250 (fits). Top 86 fine. Boss HUD maybe right top too? Unknown; boss-hud has no CSS so it renders static inside overlay? Wait #boss-hud is a div child of #battle-ui with no CSS → position static, so it appears in normal flow at top-left, possibly behind battle log. That's a pre-existing bug for boss battles! Let me check index.html for styles embedded.

Found 7 matches
/home/runner/work/PlayGround/PlayGround/styles.css:
  Line 99: .bar{height:5px;background:#1a2234;position:relative;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.5);}

  Line 101: .bar.hp > i{background:linear-gradient(90deg,#3f9e65,#7ddba0);}

  Line 102: .bar.hp.warn > i{background:linear-gradient(90deg,#b46a2a,#e8b155);}

  Line 103: .bar.hp.low > i{background:linear-gradient(90deg,#8e2737,#e35f72);}

  Line 104: .bar.mp{height:4px;}

  Line 105: .bar.mp > i{background:linear-gradient(90deg,#3a6ea8,#87c9ea);}

  Line 275: .target-card .bar{margin-top:4px;}

Indeed boss HUD lacks CSS. The dynamic JS sets `#boss-hud.hidden` removal; div would appear in flow (block) at top of #battle-ui, possibly hidden under battle log (both absolute? boss static → it's in normal flow; #battle-ui is absolute inset 0 with children absolute except boss static, so boss renders at top-left at 0,0, behind log at 14,14 with higher? log has no z-index; DOM order: log first, turn-order, boss-hud third → boss paints above log? block at top-left, maybe a mess). The user didn't mention, but "enemies disproportionate" could include boss bar. Let's add boss HUD styling: centered bottom above command? Typical boss bar top center. Add CSS:

```
.boss-hud{position:absolute;top:max(14px,env(safe-area-inset-top));left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);width:min(520px,52vw);background:rgba(7,12,23,.86);border:1px solid rgba(227,95,114,.4);padding:8px 12px;z-index:2;}
.bh-top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-family:var(--pixel);font-size:8px;color:#f0c9cf;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:6px;}
.bar.boss{height:8px;background:#2a1018;}
.bar.boss > i{display:block;height:100%;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#8e2737,#e35f72);}
```
But top center may overlap battle log (left) and turn order (right) on desktop: width 520 centered from 380..900; log 16..456; overlap 380..456. Hmm. Put boss bar below the log/turn row: top ~ 100px centered. Or bottom center above command: `bottom: 150px; left:50%` but command bottom-left height 226; center bottom 150 may overlap target layer. Top center at 108px is safer, below log height 96. Set top: 104px desktop, mobile below log 88 + turn order? On mobile, boss HUD width 86vw at top 88 might overlap turn order (top 86 right). Hide turn-order on mobile? We can place boss HUD at top 90 and turn order hidden on ≤520. On 780-520, turn order bottom 210 (old), boss top 88 fine.

Let's add CSS and mobile tweaks. Since boss bar is dynamic, this improves.

But careful not to scope creep too much. Yet boss battles are core, and currently boss HUD unstyled = definitely a bug. User mentioned two battle bugs; maybe one of them is this? "não tem botão de confirmar" and "inimigos desproporcionais" are explicit. Boss HUD is extra; fix cheaply.

Now add mobile layout CSS at end of @media (max-width...) block. Let's view the media query start to add a new separate media block at end (before max-height) or inside existing max-width:760 block. Existing `@media (max-width:760px)`? Check around line 460.

